{
  "openapi": "3.1.0",
  "info": {
    "title": "Store User Microservice API",
    "version": "1.0.0",
    "description": "User Profile Management, Account Lifecycle, and In-App Notifications Service.\nPowered by Go (Chi router), PostgreSQL (Supabase), Prisma Client Go, gRPC (Order Service Check), Apache Kafka Domain Events, and Redis Sliding-Window Rate Limiting.\n\n### Authentication & Identity Propagation\nAuthentication is performed at the API Gateway perimeter (`store_gateway`). Upon verifying valid JWT bearer credentials, the gateway injects verified headers:\n- `X-User-Id`: Authenticated User UUID (e.g. `9b1deb4d-3b7d-4bad-9bdd-2b0d7b3dcb6d`).\n- `X-User-Role`: User permission role (`customer`, `admin`).\n- `X-User-Email`: Registered email address.\n\n### Lifecycle Coordination (Account Deletion & Banning)\n- **Customer Self-Deletion (`DELETE /api/users/account`)**:\n  1. Synchronous Pre-flight Check: Queries `store_order` over gRPC (`OrderService.CheckActiveOrders`). If active orders exist (`PENDING_PAYMENT`, `PAID`, `PROCESSING`, `SHIPPED`), the deletion is blocked (`409 Conflict`).\n  2. Hard Deletion: Purges user profile from PostgreSQL.\n  3. Asynchronous Broadcast: Dispatches `user.deleted` on `user.events` with dual-compatible keys for `store_auth` token revocation and credential deletion.\n- **Admin Force Deletion (`DELETE /api/admin/users/{id}`)**:\n  - Bypasses order checks, purges profile and notifications from PostgreSQL, and broadcasts `user.deleted` with reason `admin_deletion`.\n- **Admin Account Ban (`POST /api/admin/users/{id}/ban`)**:\n  - Forcefully bans a user account while strictly preserving customer profile and notification data for audit and forensics.\n  - Broadcasts `user.banned` on `user.events` with dual-compatible keys (`event`/`event_type`, `userId`/`user_id`) to trigger token revocation in `store_auth` and order cancellation in `store_order`.\n\n### Notification Architecture Separation\n- **`store_user` (In-App Feed)**: Manages persistent user notification items in PostgreSQL (`user_notifications` table) exposed via `/api/users/notifications`.\n- **`store_notification` (Transactional Delivery)**: Dedicated microservice exclusively consuming `auth.events` to send out-of-band **OTP verification codes via Email** during registration and password resets. It does not store in-app notifications.\n\n### Rate Limiting & Resilience\n- Profile read (`GET /api/users/profile`): 60 requests per minute.\n- Profile write (`PUT /api/users/profile`): 15 requests per minute.\n- Account delete (`DELETE /api/users/account`): 3 requests per minute.\n- Admin user operations (`DELETE /api/admin/users/{id}`, `POST /api/admin/users/{id}/ban`): 15 requests per minute.\n- Notification feed read (`GET /api/users/notifications`): 60 requests per minute.\n- Notification read-status mutation & deletion: 30 requests per minute.\n- Redis sliding-window counters with fail-open fallback.\n"
  },
